{"id":"money-without-measure","title":"Money with no measured result","question":"How much of what the City pays nonprofits goes where no result recorded by someone other than the provider can be found, department by department?","finding":"Of $2.09 billion paid to nonprofits in fiscal year 2026, $1.37 billion (66%) went to providers for which no provider-level result recorded by anyone else is on disk. Published provider results exist only in Public Health (40% of its payments go to a provider with at least one published review) and Homelessness (78%). 24 departments that paid nonprofits $91.5 million have no City target for those services, no outside count and no provider result at all, led by City Administrator ($29.1 million), Arts Commission ($15.6 million), Sheriff ($12.5 million), Recreation and Parks ($6.9 million).","how":"For each department, payments to nonprofits in fiscal year 2026 are set beside: the number of City targets found for nonprofit-delivered services (first screen) and how many were met in the latest year; any count kept by an outside body; and the providers with a published monitoring result or a federal occupancy count (monitoring screen), with the share of the department's payments they received.","limits":"This measures what is published and saved on disk, not what departments know. The children's department, the early-childhood department, the housing office and the workforce office all collect results from grantees in systems that offer no download; the Human Services Agency's commission memos rarely carry a performance section. A provider counted as covered may have one small programme reviewed out of many. Departments paying under $1 million since 2019 are left out.","tier":"REDFLAG","columns":[{"k":"department","t":"Department","type":"text"},{"k":"paidFY2026","t":"Paid to nonprofits FY2026","type":"usd"},{"k":"paidSince2019","t":"Paid since FY2019","type":"usd"},{"k":"cityTargets","t":"City targets for nonprofit-delivered services"